      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Metal roofing is the superior long-term choice for Utah\u2019s harsh climate, while asphalt shingles offer a more budget-friendly upfront option.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "Metal roofing is the superior long-term choice for Utah\u2019s harsh climate, while asphalt shingles offer a more budget-friendly upfront option"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Cost Comparison"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Asphalt Shingles: Costs $10,000 to $18,000 installed. They provide a lower initial investment and lower labor costs."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Metal Roofing: Costs $20,000 to $40,000 or more installed. It is typically 2 to 3 times more expensive upfront than asphalt, but breaks down to a lower cost per year if you stay in your home long-term."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          2,
          3
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Lifespan and Durability"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Asphalt Shingles: Lasts 20 to 30 years. Granules loosen over time from intense UV rays and freeze-thaw cycles, leading to cracking and edge lifting.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              4
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Metal Roofing: Lasts 40 to 70 years. It resists high winds, intense sun, fire, and hail much better than asphalt, though thicker gauges (like 24-gauge over 26-gauge) are recommended to prevent denting or oil-canning."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          5,
          6
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Performance in Utah Weather"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Snow and Ice: Utah winters\u2014especially in mountain or northern regions\u2014bring heavy snow. Metal's slick, vertical panels naturally shed snow and reduce the risk of ice damming. Asphalt's textured surface traps moisture and ice, putting more physical strain on the roof.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              7
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Energy Efficiency: Metal reflects solar heat during hot Utah summers, lowering cooling costs. Asphalt absorbs and retains heat."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "HOA and Rules: Asphalt shingles are universally accepted by HOAs. Metal roofing may face restrictions or require specific architectural styles in certain neighborhoods."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          8
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like to narrow this down, tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Where in Utah\nis your home located?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "How long do you plan to live there?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Does your neighborhood have an HOA?"
          }
        ]
      }
